工作职责:
Candidates will be assigned to either underwriting or claims based on your educational background and career goals.

As a Property and Liability Insurance Underwriter, you will:
1. Assist senior underwriters in business acceptance and review;
2. To learn and understand the knowledge of property and liability insurance products, collect and organize relevant business data to support business analysis and decision making;
3. Participate in business process optimization and improvement to enhance work efficiency and service quality.

As a Marine Insurance Underwriter, you will: 
1. Marine/logistics insurance business auditing, risk assessment, execution in accordance with company underwriting policy;
2. General clerical work and filing of documents;
3. Production and analysis of relevant statistics;
4. Produce and analyze relevant statistics.

As an Insurance Claims Handler, you will:
1. Provide advice on making a claim and the processes involved;
2. Collect accurate information and documents to proceed with a claim;
3. Analyse a claim made by a policymaker to establish whether it satisfies the policy conditions;
4. Guide policyholders on how to proceed with the claim;
5. Contact service provider from a network of approved professionals;
6. Monitor the progress of a claim;
7. Ensure fair settlement of a valid claim.

